  "templateDeviations": [
    {
      "id": "no-information-model",
      "clause": "7 to 13, Annex A",
      "statement": "This document defines a DataEncoding: a mapping of the OPC UA type model onto Apache Avro, and of the OPC UA PubSub messages onto Avro-encoded payloads. It defines no OPC UA information model of its own: it has no NodeSet, no ObjectTypes, no VariableTypes, no DataTypes, no ReferenceTypes and no Instances. The NodeClass clauses of OPC 20020 are therefore omitted rather than left empty, and Annex A states the generated type reference this document does define in place of a NodeSet."
    }
  ],
  "identity": {
    "docNumber": "OPC nnnnn-m",
    "partNumber": "Part 1",
    "partName": "Avro Encoding",
    "title": "Avro Encoding",
    "subjectTerm": "Avro",
    "mainTitle": "OPC UA FOR APACHE AVRO ENCODING",
    "subTitle": "Part 1: Binary DataEncoding and PubSub message mapping",
    "shortName": "AVRO",
    "capabilityIdentifier": "AVRO",
    "namespaceUri": "http://opcfoundation.org/UA/",
    "namespaceIndexInDocument": 0,
    "annexASubject": "DataEncoding",
    "version": "0.1.0",
    "publicationDate": "2026-07-30",
    "releaseType": "Draft",
    "mantisProjectId": "<nnn>",
    "otherOrganization": "Apache Software Foundation",
    "introduction": [
      "Apache Avro is a compact binary serialization format in which the data carries no type information of its own. A writer encodes values against a schema, and a reader can only decode them by holding that same schema, so a message is a small payload plus a way of naming the schema that produced it. Because nothing is repeated per value, the encoded form is a fraction of the size of a self-describing one.",
      "That trade suits OPC UA. A Server publishing a DataSet many times a second repeats the same structure every time, and both the OPC UA binary and the JSON encoding carry that structure on the wire. Avro moves it out of the message and into a schema resolved once.",
      "This document defines how the OPC UA type model maps onto Avro, how a schema is generated deterministically from a NodeSet or from DataSetMetaData so that two implementations produce the same schema and therefore the same identity for it, and how a PubSub NetworkMessage, DataSetMessage, Action and Discovery message are carried in Avro form."
    ],
    "draftBanner": "PROVISIONAL WORKING DRAFT — not normative, not endorsed by the OPC Foundation. The document number and the Mantis project identifier in this document are placeholders; the OPC Foundation assigns the real values."
  },
  "_comment_prose": "Clauses the template requires that this document has no material shaped like.",
  "prose": {
    "conformance": [
      "Conformance is composed from independently implementable conformance units. An implementation claims AVRO-DataEncoding at minimum; the remaining units build on it and may be claimed separately.",
      "AVRO-DataEncoding — the mapping of the OPC UA type model onto Avro, in both directions, including the reversibility requirement that decoding an encoded value yields the original value.",
      "AVRO-SchemaGeneration — deterministic schema generation from a NodeSet or from DataSetMetaData, and the SchemaId that identifies the result. Two conforming implementations given the same input produce the same schema and the same SchemaId.",
      "AVRO-SchemaResolution — decoder-side schema resolution, including cache-miss behaviour and the schema-evolution rules that let a writer add fields without breaking a deployed reader.",
      "AVRO-PubSub — the NetworkMessage and DataSetMessage mapping, the SchemaId handshake, the configuration parameters and the transport content types.",
      "AVRO-Actions — the Action invoke and response messages and the Discovery messages.",
      "A Server that publishes Avro-encoded DataSets claims AVRO-DataEncoding, AVRO-SchemaGeneration and AVRO-PubSub. A Client that consumes them claims AVRO-DataEncoding and AVRO-SchemaResolution."
    ]
  },
